1
00:00:00,225 --> 00:00:01,265
And, um...

2
00:00:01,435 --> 00:00:05,645
(Sheldon:)I can tie a string to your leg
and fly you like a kite.

3
00:00:05,814 --> 00:00:08,404
(Amy:)If you're keeping him,
I've got a cage you can borrow.

4
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:12,527
(Amy:)One of the test monkeys slipped
on a banana peel and broke his neck.

5
00:00:13,113 --> 00:00:16,203
(Amy:)It was both tragic and hysterical.

6
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:22,619
Nonsense. No, Lovey Dovey
doesn't sleep in a cage.

7
00:00:22,831 --> 00:00:26,121
No, Lovey Dovey sleeps
in his very own nest...

8
00:00:26,335 --> 00:00:29,835
(Sheldon:)...which I'm going to get off
the window sill and put in my room.

9
00:00:30,005 --> 00:00:32,505
(Sheldon:)Isn't that right, L.D.?

10
00:00:36,637 --> 00:00:37,807
(Penny:)No.

11
00:00:37,971 --> 00:00:39,431
(Sheldon:)Where are you going?

12
00:00:39,598 --> 00:00:43,018
Come back, Lovey Dovey.
This is your home now.

13
00:00:43,185 --> 00:00:47,275
(Sheldon:)I already ordered 20 pounds
of bird feed off of Amazon.

14
00:00:49,108 --> 00:00:52,448
(Leonard:)- He's gone.
- I'm sorry, Sheldon.

15
00:00:52,611 --> 00:00:54,571
(Sheldon:)How could he do this to me?

16
00:00:55,405 --> 00:01:35,025
(Sheldon:)Get back here you stupid bird
so I can Iove you!

